  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;square in the figure. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>49</mn></msub></math> be the points of intersections (dots in the picture) in some order. We say that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math> are friends if they are adjacent along a row or along a column. Assume that each point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math> has an equal chance of being chosen.</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0002_ef3c1e49bb0c.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 197px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>(There are two questions based on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PARAGRAPH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#34;</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></math>, the question given below is one of them)</p>\n<br>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math> be the probability that a randomly chosen point has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi></math> many friends, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> be a random variable such that for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, the probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "24",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Plotting the diagram of the given data we get,<img src=\"assets\\st0004_721b011d8343.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 256px;\" /></p><p>Now from above diagram we get,</p><p>Number of points having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> friend <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Number of points having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> friend <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Number of points having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> friends <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />Number of points having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> friends <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p>Number of points having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> friends&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p>So, probability distribution table will be,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0004_bab08d9ef2b6.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 74px;\" /></p><p>Now from above table expected value will be given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>E</mi><mfenced><mi>X</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>49</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>49</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>49</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>E</mi><mfenced><mi>X</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>49</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>E</mi><mfenced><mi>X</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}